<title>JAPAN: Japan August pork imports down 46.5 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan August pork imports down 46.5 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's pork imports in August totalled 28,449 tonnes, down 46.5 percent from 53,155 tonnes in August 1995, Finance Ministry data released on Monday showed.</p>
<p>Details were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		   August 96     July 96     August 95</p>
<p> Total	     28,449	 40,775	 53,155</p>
<p> Refrigerated    15,835	 15,604	 18,045</p>
<p> Frozen	    12,614	 25,171	 35,110</p>
<p>Major suppliers of refrigerated pork (in tonnes):</p>
<p> Taiwan	     8,040	  7,585	  8,412</p>
<p> U.S.		 6,733	  6,864	  8,784</p>
<p>Major supplier of frozen pork (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    August 96	July 96	August 95</p>
<p> Taiwan	     4,602	 10,681	 14,925</p>
<p>Imports of refrigerated pork in the first eight months of calendar 1996 totalled 116,541 tonnes, against 108,621 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>Imports of frozen pork in the first eight months of calendar 1996 came to 391,682 tonnes, against 257,432 tonnes in the same period of 1995, ministry data showed.</p>
</text>
